WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
BUILD 082. AN AUDIENCE IS NOT A DEMOGRAPHIC BOX.. A fictional persona card cannot explain a relationship, and demographic proxies cannot supply the missing context.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
EXPAND THE CARD INTO A GRAPH. NEED · LANGUAGE · CONTEXT. Fixed synthetic sources connect to ontology nodes while evidence, caveats, and unknowns remain attached.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
DESCRIBE THE RELATIONSHIPS. SOURCE · EVIDENCE · UNKNOWN. Edges record bounded fixture relationships rather than inferred identity, personality, protected traits, or behavior.

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
KEEP CLAIM TYPES SEPARATE. TRUST · INFLUENCE · ACTION. Trusted-source assertions and conversion evidence retain explicit caveats; neither becomes a prediction.

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
BOUND THE RESULT. A GRAPH DOES NOT DEFINE PEOPLE. Fixed synthetic audience only; no profiling, targeting, persuasion, surveillance, demographic, protected-trait, identity, psychographic, trustworthiness, influence, behavior, or conversion inference.

6
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
SAVE THIS. UNDERSTAND THE RELATIONSHIPS.. CONNECT NEED, LANGUAGE, AND CONTEXT. RETAIN SOURCE, EVIDENCE, CAVEAT, CONTRADICTION, CHANGE, AND UNKNOWN.

